l","H1840","HNpm","Daniel"],["עַד","'ad-","H5704","HR","until"],["שְׁנַת","shenat","H8141","HNcfsc","year"],["אַחַת","'achat","H259","HAcfsa","one"],["לְכוֹרֶשׁ","lekhoresh","H3566","HR/Npm","of Cyrus"],["הַמֶּלֶךְ","hamelekh","H4428","HTd/Ncmsa","the king"]],"x":[[27006028,27006028,7],[27010001,27010001,6]],"xn":2}},"people":[{"id":"nebuchadnezzar_2167","name":"Nebuchadnezzar","also":"Nebuchadrezzar","summary":"In the Babylonian orthography Nabu-kudur-uzur, which means “Nebo, protect the crown!” or the “frontiers.” In an inscription he styles himself “Nebo’s favourite.”","verses":88,"father":"","mother":"","v":[1,18]},{"id":"jehoiakim_1085","name":"Jehoiakim","also":"Eliakim","summary":"He whom Jehovah has set up, the second son of Josiah, and eighteenth king of Judah, which he ruled over for eleven years (B.C. 610-599).","verses":37,"father":"Josiah","mother":"Zebudah","v":[1,2]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[3]},{"id":"ashpenaz_339","name":"Ashpenaz","also":"","summary":"The master of the eunuchs of Nebuchadnezzar (Dan. 1:3), the “Rabsaris” of the court.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[3]},{"id":"daniel_975","name":"Daniel","also":"Belteshazzar","summary":"Beltis protect the king!, the Chaldee name given to Daniel by Nebuchadnezzar (Dan. 1:7).","verses":72,"father":"","mother":"","v":[6,7,8,9,10,11,17,19,21]},{"id":"meshach_2092","name":"Meshach","also":"Mishael","summary":"One of the three Hebrew youths who were trained with Daniel in Babylon (Dan. 1:11, 19), and promoted to the rank of Magi. He and his companions were afterwards cast into the burning fiery furnace for refusing to worship the idol the king had set up, from which they were miraculously delivered (3:13-30).","verses":18,"father":"","mother":"","v":[6,7,11,19]},{"id":"shadrach_1398","name":"Shadrach","also":"Hananiah","summary":"Aku’s command, the Chaldean name given to Hananiah, one of the Hebrew youths whom Nebuchadnezzar carried captive to Babylon (Dan. 1:6, 7; 3:12-30).","verses":18,"father":"","mother":"","v":[6,7,11,19]},{"id":"azariah_545","name":"Azariah","also":"","summary":"The original name of Abed-nego (Dan. 1:6, 7, 11, 16).","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[6,7,11,19]},{"id":"melzar_1994","name":"Melzar","also":"","summary":"Probably a Persian word meaning master of wine, i.e., chief butler; the title of an officer at the Babylonian court (Dan. 1:11, 16) who had charge of the diet of the Hebrew youths.","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[11,16]},{"id":"cyrus_968","name":"Cyrus","also":"","summary":"(Heb. Ko’resh), the celebrated “King of Persia” (Elam) who was conqueror of Babylon, and issued the decree of liberation to the Jews (Ezra 1:1, 2).","verses":19,"father":"","mother":"","v":[21]}],"places":[{"id":"babylon_151","name":"Babylon","kind":"City","lat":32.53617,"lon":44.42082,"summary":"The Greek form of BABEL; Semitic form Babilu, meaning “The Gate of God.” In the Assyrian tablets it means “The city of the dispersion of the tribes.”","verses":255,"v":[1]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[1]},{"id":"shinar_1084","name":"Shinar","kind":"Region","lat":32.5365,"lon":44.42088,"summary":"LXX. and Vulgate “Senaar;” in the inscriptions, “Shumir;” probably identical with Babylonia or Southern Mesopotamia, extending almost to the Persian Gulf.","verses":8,"v":[2]}],"events":[{"id":"prophecies_of_daniel_240","title":"Prophecies of Daniel","year":-606,"summary":"Passa